class:: Gendreve
summary:: Mean-reverting chaotic breakpoint oscillator
related:: Classes/Diststoch, Classes/Chaosgen
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic

description::

A ring of code::knum:: control points traversed at audio rate. Each point carries its
own kicked-rotor map, so its value is deterministic chaos rather than a random walk,
and each is pulled back toward a template shape by the two emphasis::stiffness::
parameters.

The tether scales the chaotic deviation instead of contracting the map state, so
raising a stiffness morphs continuously from chaos to the bare template without damping
the chaos out. At code::ampStiffness = 1:: the output is exactly the template.

code::ampKick:: and code::durKick:: set the rotor kick: below roughly 1 the map is
quasi-periodic, above it chaotic, with periodic windows scattered through the range.

Two outputs: the signal, and a template-locked reference, so code::out[0] - out[1]:: is
the chaotic residual. code::knum:: is fixed at build time.

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: minfreq
Lower fundamental bound (Hz).
argument:: maxfreq
Upper fundamental bound (Hz).
argument:: knum
Control points (fixed). Default 12.
argument:: ampStiffness
Pull toward the template, 0–1. 1 = exactly the template. Default 0.1.
argument:: durStiffness
Pull toward code::centerDur::, 0–1. 1 = locked pitch. Default 0.1.
argument:: ampKick
Amplitude rotor kick. Chaotic above ~1. Default 2.0.
argument:: durKick
Duration rotor kick. Default 2.0.
argument:: templateType
0 sine, 1 saw, 2 triangle, 3 square, 4 flat. Default 0.
argument:: templateSkew
Pulse width, 0–1. Default 0.5.
argument:: centerDur
Reference pitch position, 0–1. Default 0.5.
argument:: interp
0 hold, 1 linear, 2 cosine. Default 1.
argument:: mul
argument:: add

examples::
code::
{ Gendreve.ar(150, 150, 12, MouseX.kr(0, 1), 1.0, 2.0, 2.0)[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

{ Gendreve.ar(100, 400, 12, MouseX.kr(0, 1), MouseY.kr(0, 1), 2.0, 2.0)[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

{ Gendreve.ar(150, 150, 12, 0.1, 1.0, MouseX.kr(0.2, 8), 2.0)[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

{ Gendreve.ar(80, 400, 12, 0.3, 0.0, 2.0, 2.0, 1)[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

{ var g = Gendreve.ar(120, 120, 16, 0.35, 1.0, 3.0, 2.0, 2);
  (g[0] - g[1]) * 0.3 ! 2 }.play;

{ Gendreve.ar(60, 240, 24, MouseX.kr(0, 0.9), 0.6, 4.0, 1.5, 3, 0.25, 0.4, 2)[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

{ Gendreve.ar(200, 200, 8, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 2.0, 0, 0.5, 0.5, 0)[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

{ Gendreve.ar(90, 90, 20, SinOsc.kr(0.07).range(0, 0.95), 1.0, 2.5, 2.0, 1)[0] * 0.25 ! 2 }.play;
::
